<!--
    kuna `pow2select`: clang selects with csel / csneg on AArch64.  Signed
    `x / 4` is `v = x + 3; if (0 <= x) v = x; return v >> 2;` and `x % 8` is
    `v = x & 7; if (0 <= -x) v = -(-x & 7);` (for `x % 2`, `-(x & 1)`).  With
    the option on (the default) the division prints as `x / 4` and the
    MULTIEQUAL of the remainder as `x % 8`, when the branch provably sends
    every positive x to one input and every negative x to the other.

    Stage / sub-stage: P3 "simplification-quiescence", option
    `pow2select on|off`.

    The bytes are the .text of decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/
    pow2select.c built by clang 22.1 for aarch64-linux-gnu at -O2 (an object file),
    placed at 0x100000.  near4 selects `-(-x & 7)` for x < -4 only, which is
    not a remainder for x in -4..-1, and keeps its select.  Pass 1 is the
    default, pass 2 `option pow2select off`.
-->
